<title>FRANCE: Seita drops on French cancer lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Seita drops on French cancer lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French tobacco group Seita fell on Thursday after a cancer victim sued it for a lack of information on the dangers of smoking, traders said.</p>
<p>The case is the first of its kind in France.</p>
<p>The plaintiff, who is claiming two million francs in damages, alleges his cancer came from smoking Gauloise cigarettes, Seita said. The company said it is confident it will win the case and pointed out that no money has been paid out anywhere in such cases, especially the United States where a number of actions have been brought.</p>
<p>Seita fell 0.38 percent to 212 francs at 1047 GMT.</p>
</text>
